<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Government of India</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Union Government of India</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> is the union government of the Republic of India, seated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-delhi">New Delhi</a> and constituted since 1950 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a>. Its executive consists of the president and the council of ministers headed by the prime minister, responsible to Parliament; after independence in 1947 it integrated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> into the Indian Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/government-of-india.jpg" alt="Government of India" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
